From 0ab52488114341c67d89ffa107af281d60146e77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:36:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] .17 Decision/Execution Ledger: required-vs-optional
 symbol handling for full coin universe

Same pattern as .13-.16: REQUIRED_SYMBOLS (BTC/ETH) remain the only
symbols whose structural invalidity can block the whole ledger decision.
Every other symbol .16 reports -- including one .16 itself individually
blocked -- gets its own ledger entry independently.

Specific changes:
- New ledger_entry_errors_for_symbol(symbol, item) helper factors out the
  original per-symbol structural checks (valid execution_decision, intent
  flag consistency, no fabricated fill price/timestamp, no position
  claim). "BLOCKED" was already an accepted execution_decision value in
  this check, so an optional symbol .16 individually blocked needs no
  special-casing here.
- verify_upstream()'s structural-validity loop scoped to REQUIRED_SYMBOLS
  only; the intent-count used to cross-check .16's own
  paper_execution_allowed / overall_execution_decision fields now spans
  the FULL symbol set (required + optional), matching how .16 itself
  already counts any symbol's intent toward those aggregate fields --
  without this, a legitimate optional-symbol intent would look like an
  upstream inconsistency and wrongly block everything.
- build_ledger()'s main loop iterates every symbol .16 reported (union
  with REQUIRED_SYMBOLS): required symbols keep the original recording
  logic; optional symbols get the same plus a distinct
  UPSTREAM_EXECUTION_BLOCKED reason when passing through a legitimate
  upstream block, recorded in optional_symbols_blocked, without affecting
  the required pair.
- print_report() iterates actual decisions instead of a fixed BTC/ETH
  tuple, labeling each symbol REQUIRED/OPTIONAL.

Adds 9 contract tests, including the intent-count cross-check now
spanning optional symbols and an optional-structural-inconsistency-
blocks-only-that-symbol test. Full suite (60 tests) green.

